title: Soul_FirstAwakening
tags: npc milestone progression
---
// Triggers after player survives Wave 5. The Heartwood pulses bright. A figure materializes at its base.
<<play_sfx heartwood_pulse_major>>
<<camera_focus heartwood>>
<<wait 2>>

// Golden light gathers. A human form emerges from the bark — disoriented, blinking, alive.
<<spawn_npc blacksmith at heartwood>>
<<play_sfx soul_emerge>>
<<wait 2>>

{$companionName}: Wait — look at the tree.

{$companionName}: Someone's coming through.

<<wait 1>>

Aldric: ...where... how long has it been?

{$companionName}: Easy. Take your time.

Aldric: I was... we were in the tree. All of us. I could hear the others. Feel them.

Aldric: The Heartwood — it's stronger now. Strong enough to let me out.

-> Who are you?
    Aldric: My name is Aldric. I was the village blacksmith. Before... before the end.
    Aldric: When the last wall fell, I put my hands on the bark like everyone else. My wife. My daughter. We all went in together.
    Aldric: They're still in there. I can feel them. But the tree isn't strong enough yet. Only one at a time.
-> Are you alright?
    Aldric: I'm alive. I think. It's been... centuries? The memories inside the tree — they blur together.
    Aldric: But I remember the forge. My hammer. The sound of iron on the anvil.
    Aldric: And I remember my family. They're still waiting.

<<wait 1>>

Aldric: You did this. You defended the tree long enough for it to grow. For me to come back.

Aldric: I owe you more than I can say.

<<wait 0.5>>

Aldric: Take this.

<<play_sfx spirit_bond>>

Aldric: My spirit companion — a Grimhound. He stayed with me through the darkness inside the tree. He's loyal. Tireless.

Aldric: He'll gather for you. Fight for you. Whatever you need.

<<grant_pet grimhound "Aldric's Grimhound">>

Aldric: Use him well. The faster we grow the Heartwood, the sooner my wife and daughter can come home.

<<wait 1>>

Aldric: I'll set up at the Forge. It's the only thing I know how to do. And this village needs weapons.

{$companionName}: Aldric... welcome back.

Aldric: Don't welcome me yet. Not until they're all back.

<<set $soulsFreed to 1>>
<<set $aldricFreed to true>>
<<move_npc aldric to forge>>
===

title: Soul_SecondAwakening
tags: npc milestone progression
---
// Triggers after player survives Wave 10. Second soul emerges.
<<play_sfx heartwood_pulse_major>>
<<camera_focus heartwood>>
<<wait 2>>

<<spawn_npc merchant at heartwood>>
<<play_sfx soul_emerge>>

{$companionName}: Another one. The tree is getting stronger.

Mira: Aldric? Is that you at the forge? I can smell the coal from here.

Aldric: Mira! You're out!

Mira: It seems our Defender has been busy.

<<wait 1>>

Mira: I was a trader. Before. I knew every road, every merchant route in the old kingdom.

Mira: Those roads are gone now. But trade... trade I can still do.

-> Welcome to Elarion.
    Mira: Elarion. Is that what they call it now? It used to be Elarion the Golden. But I suppose we start where we are.
-> Are there others still inside?
    Mira: Hundreds. Thousands. I could hear them in the dark. Voices. Children singing. Old men telling stories.
    Mira: They're patient. They've waited centuries. But every soul you free gives the rest hope.
    Mira: Don't stop.

<<wait 0.5>>

Mira: Here — take my spirit companion. A Windrider Hawk.

<<play_sfx spirit_bond>>

Mira: She sees everything from above. Hidden nodes, enemy camps, paths you'd never find on foot.

Mira: Let her scout for you. The more you find out there, the faster this village grows. The faster they come home.

<<grant_pet hawk "Mira's Hawk">>

Mira: I'll set up in the Market. Someone needs to make sure all these resources go where they're needed.

<<set $soulsFreed to 2>>
<<set $miraFreed to true>>
<<move_npc mira to market>>
===

title: Soul_ThirdAwakening
tags: npc milestone progression
---
// Triggers after player survives Wave 15.
<<play_sfx heartwood_pulse_major>>
<<camera_focus heartwood>>
<<wait 2>>

<<spawn_npc scholar at heartwood>>
<<play_sfx soul_emerge>>

{$companionName}: A third. The Heartwood is blooming.

Elowen: The stars... they've moved. How long were we inside?

{$companionName}: Long enough. But you're here now.

Elowen: I was keeper of the Arcane Tower. I studied the World Ash — its energy, its connections to every living thing.

Elowen: I thought I understood it. Then it fell, and I understood nothing.

-> What can you teach us?
    Elowen: Everything I learned before the Sundering. How to channel the Heartwood's energy. How to bind elemental power into your towers.
    Elowen: That Flame Tower of yours? I can make it burn hotter. Your Ballista? I can enchant the bolts.
    Elowen: The tree's power is growing. Let me help you use it.
-> How many souls are left?
    Elowen: I could sense them. In the quiet moments, when the tree slept, we'd count each other.
    Elowen: Thousands. Families. Whole neighborhoods. Children who never got to grow up.
    Elowen: Every wave you survive, the tree reaches a little deeper. One more soul rises.
    Elowen: We don't need an army. We need time. And someone to hold the walls while the tree does its work.

<<wait 0.5>>

Elowen: My spirit companion. A Thornback Boar.

<<play_sfx spirit_bond>>

Elowen: Stubborn creature. Won't stop working until the job is done. Reminds me of myself.

Elowen: He'll haul resources faster than any two workers. Put him to use.

<<grant_pet boar "Elowen's Boar">>

Elowen: I'll be at the Arcane Tower. There's research to resume. Centuries of it.

<<set $soulsFreed to 3>>
<<set $elowenFreed to true>>
<<move_npc elowen to arcane_tower>>
===

title: Soul_FourthAwakening
tags: npc milestone progression
---
// Triggers after player survives Wave 20.
<<play_sfx heartwood_pulse_major>>
<<camera_focus heartwood>>
<<wait 2>>

<<spawn_npc healer at heartwood>>
<<play_sfx soul_emerge>>

{$companionName}: Four now. I'm starting to remember what a real village feels like.

Senna: Is it safe? Are the walls holding?

{$companionName}: They are. Because of our Defender.

Senna: Then it wasn't for nothing. None of it was for nothing.

<<wait 1>>

Senna: I was a healer. I was the last one treating the wounded when the final wall fell.

Senna: I held a dying soldier's hand and pressed my other hand to the bark. We went in together.

-> Is he still in there?
    Senna: Yes. Tomas. He's waiting. They all are.
    Senna: But the tree is so much stronger now. I can feel it reaching. Searching for the next soul to release.
    Senna: Every battle you win, every tower you build — it's not just defense. It's a rescue.
-> We'll get them out.
    Senna: I believe you. Three others came before me, and the village already looks... alive again.
    Senna: That's what the Heartwood needs. Not just protection. Life. Purpose. Noise.
    Senna: The souls inside can feel it. When you build, they stir. When you fight, they wake. When you celebrate a victory... I swear I heard them singing.

<<wait 0.5>>

Senna: Take him. My Stonebear.

<<play_sfx spirit_bond>>

Senna: He kept me warm in the darkness. Strong enough to carry anything. Stubborn enough to stand when everything falls.

Senna: Sound like anyone you know?

<<grant_pet bear "Senna's Stonebear">>

Senna: I'll set up near the Heartwood. Someone needs to tend to it — and to you, after those battles.

<<set $soulsFreed to 4>>
<<set $sennaFreed to true>>
<<move_npc senna to heartwood_shrine>>
===

title: Soul_FifthAwakening
tags: npc milestone progression
---
// Triggers after player survives Wave 30. The big one.
<<play_sfx heartwood_pulse_massive>>
<<camera_shake 0.5>>
<<camera_focus heartwood>>
<<wait 3>>

// The tree glows brighter than ever before. Multiple lights swirl inside the bark.
<<play_sfx souls_chorus>>

{$companionName}: Something's happening. Something big.

<<wait 2>>

// A figure emerges — older, regal. Not disoriented. Calm. Eyes open and clear.
<<spawn_npc elder at heartwood>>
<<play_sfx soul_emerge_major>>

Elder Varen: You've done well, Defender.

{$companionName}: Who...?

Elder Varen: My name is Varen. I was the last Elder of the Verdant Watch.

Elder Varen: I was the one who gave the order. When the walls fell, when there was nothing left — I told them to touch the tree.

<<wait 1>>

Elder Varen: Every soul that went in... that was my responsibility. My promise that someday, someone would come.

-> They came back. You kept your promise.
    Elder Varen: Four have returned. But there are thousands more. And the tree... it's still fragile.
    Elder Varen: Every soul it releases costs it strength. We must defend it harder, build it stronger, so it can keep giving them back.
    Elder Varen: The work doesn't get easier from here. It gets heavier.
-> What happens when they're all free?
    Elder Varen: Then Elarion lives again. Not as it was — nothing is ever as it was.
    Elder Varen: But as something new. Built by the hands of someone who showed up when no one else would.
    Elder Varen: The Echoes won't just be memories anymore. They'll be people. Families. A civilization reborn.
    Elder Varen: And you — you'll be the one who made it possible. Not through power. Through persistence.

<<wait 1>>

Elder Varen: I don't have a spirit animal to give you. I gave mine to the tree long ago — it became the Heartwood's first guardian.

Elder Varen: But I can give you something else.

<<play_sfx ancient_power>>

Elder Varen: The knowledge of the Verdant Watch. Every technique, every ward, every defense we ever devised.

Elder Varen: Your towers will be stronger. Your walls will hold longer. The Heartwood will grow faster.

<<grant_elder_blessing>>

Elder Varen: I'll stay at the tree. I promised I'd be the last one out, and I'll keep that promise.

Elder Varen: Bring them home, Defender. All of them.

<<set $soulsFreed to 5>>
<<set $varenFreed to true>>
<<set $elderBlessingActive to true>>
===

title: Soul_Progress_Check
tags: companion ambient contextual
---
// Companion comments on soul progress when player visits the Heartwood
<<if $soulsFreed == 1>>
    {$companionName}: One soul freed. The tree gave everything to push Aldric out. It needs time to recover before the next one.
    {$companionName}: Keep defending. Keep building. The tree grows from our effort, not from magic.
<<elseif $soulsFreed == 2>>
    {$companionName}: Two souls. Aldric and Mira. A blacksmith and a trader. Elarion is starting to feel like a real place again.
<<elseif $soulsFreed == 3>>
    {$companionName}: Three souls free. I can feel the tree reaching deeper. The next one is close.
    {$companionName}: The more we build, the faster it grows. Every wall, every tower — it all feeds the Heartwood.
<<elseif $soulsFreed == 4>>
    {$companionName}: Four souls. The village has a blacksmith, a trader, a scholar, and a healer. That's not a camp anymore. That's a town.
    {$companionName}: But there are thousands still waiting. We're not done.
<<elseif $soulsFreed >= 5>>
    {$companionName}: The Elder himself. Varen. The one who put them all in the tree.
    {$companionName}: If he's out... the tree is strong. Really strong.
    {$companionName}: Keep going. Every wave survived. Every resource gathered. Every Echo tamed. It all matters.
<<endif>>
===
